  "id": "COMPOUND:43386 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Nardostachin is implicated in the biological activity of SCCH-26 through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Nardostachin to Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which is targeted by 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, a compound that ultimately targets SCCH-26. The second pathway connects Nardostachin to Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is targeted by Cassialactone, another compound that also targets SCCH-26. These pathways suggest that Nardostachin may influence SCCH-26 through distinct molecular mechanisms, possibly involving protein modification or structural changes in the cell. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Nardostachin to modulate SCCH-26 via different molecular targets, emphasizing the complexity of its interaction with the cell. The evidence supports a role for Nardostachin in modulating SCCH-26 through multiple, yet interconnected, molecular mechanisms.",
